## General

- Use explicit naming for variables (eg: `index` instead of `i`, `source` instead of `src`, `image` instead of `img`, `directory` instead of `dir`)
- Always use typing annotation
- Always include complete docstrings, eg:
    ```
    """Initialize attributes of the model

    Args:
        model_name (str): The name of the model, to be loaded from Hugging Face
        load_in_4bit (bool): Whether to load the model in 4-bit. Optional, defaults to True.
        device_map (str): The device map to use for the model. Optional, defaults to "auto".
        max_seq_length (int): The maximum sequence length to use for the model. Optional, defaults to 2048.
    """
    ```
    When there's a default argument specifity it with `Optional, defaults to ...`

- If possible try to always split a function logically in sub functions (where it makes sense), so that we keep complexity of functions < 10

## Documentation
- Use Google-style docstrings
- Document all public APIs
- Keep README.md updated
- Use proper inline comments
- Generate API documentation
- Document environment setup

